    "background_story": "Sutton was a detective with a keen mind and a sharp instinct for solving the most heinous crimes. His latest case was a particularly gruesome murder that had shaken the small town of Ravenswood to its core. The victim, a young socialite, had been found dead in her mansion with no signs of forced entry or struggle. As Sutton delved deeper into the investigation, he uncovered a web of secrets and lies that led him to suspect the victim's own family members. With each new discovery, Sutton's determination to bring justice to the victim grew. He worked tirelessly, following every lead, every clue, until he finally uncovered the shocking truth. The killer was none other than the victim's own brother, driven by a twisted desire for inheritance. Sutton's relentless pursuit of justice had solved the case, but the darkness of the crime would stay with him forever.",
